  "publishedAt": null,
  "contentHtml": "<figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!w6Is!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5de5d442-0449-4f37-a82b-7e09457b3074_2756x748.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n<img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!w6Is!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F5de5d442-0449-4f37-a82b-7e09457b3074_2756x748.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"395\" data-size=\"normal\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n\n</a></figure>\n<p>In this space on Saturdays, I <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/t/roundup\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">do a weekly round-up</a> of sorts: Sifting through what I wrote that you might have missed during the week, what I’ve been reading and watching myself, and some other fun things that have been going on.</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/subscribe?\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><span>Subscribe now</span></a></p>\n<hr>\n<h4>📝 What I did this week</h4>\n<p><em>Here are the things I wrote or podcasted about during the previous week, sorted in descending order by quality, popularity and/or current relevance.</em></p>\n<p><strong>📊 My <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/t/updating-model\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Odds/Models</a>: <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-nfl-odds-tracker-and-elo-ratings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NFL </a></strong>| <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-mlb-elo-power-ratings-playoff\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">MLB </a></strong>| <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-wnba-elo-team-power-rankings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">WNBA </a></strong>| <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-27-nba-elo-forecast-and-player\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NBA</a></strong> | <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-27-nhl-team-elo-power-rankings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NHL </a></strong>| <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-college-football-odds-tracker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">CFB</a></strong> | <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-27-english-premier-league-tracker\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">EPL</a> | <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-nascar-cup-series-driver-rankings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">NASCAR</a></strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Check out the <strong><a href=\"https://view.newsletters.yahoo.net/messages/1793360738484aa845bd911d1/raw\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Yahoo! Sports AM newsletter</a></strong> for my various charts and other contributions, including…</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://view.newsletters.yahoo.net/messages/1793360738484aa845bd911d1/raw#:~:text=ROARING%20BRUINS%2C%20QUIET%20CROWDS\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Roaring bruins, quiet crowds</a> </strong>- Despite being undefeated and ranked No. 7 in the nation, UCLA football is suffering from surprisingly low attendance at the Rose Bowl:</p>\n<div class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/GRk2R/1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/43a9fe00-0a48-41da-8cae-3be3e07c88a2_1220x1264.png\" alt=\"UCLA is an attendance outlier\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>UCLA is an attendance outlier</p></div>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://view.newsletters.yahoo.net/messages/17932796664191a45cc90353e/raw#:~:text=Welcome%20to%20the%20club%3A\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Welcome to the club</a></strong> - With the Brewers winning, now there are only four MLB teams still waiting to check off their box on the “bingo card” of champions:</p>\n<figure><a href=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!wEJL!,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0eef120b-5fc0-4f7c-81c1-8d8026764fb9_1900x1599.png\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">\n<img src=\"https://substackcdn.com/image/fetch/%24s_!wEJL!,w_1456,c_limit,f_auto,q_auto:good,fl_progressive:steep/https%3A%2F%2Fsubstack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com%2Fpublic%2Fimages%2F0eef120b-5fc0-4f7c-81c1-8d8026764fb9_1900x1599.png\" width=\"1456\" height=\"1225\" data-size=\"normal\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\">\n\n\n</a></figure>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong><a href=\"https://view.newsletters.yahoo.net/messages/1793101944790e19ea72be938/raw#:~:text=HEISMAN%20WATCH%3A%20A%20TRIO%20OF%20ELITE%20WRs\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Heisman Watch: A Trio of Elite WRs</a></strong> - Oregon State’s Jesse Legree, Ohio State’s Jeremiah Smith and Miami’s Malachi Toney are racking up yards at historic receiving paces:</p>\n<div class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/IULYg/2/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/6a49514c-6b59-4774-a037-dc2a76c1798f_1220x1498.png\" alt=\"Smith, Toney and (especially) Legree are piling up the yards\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>Smith, Toney and (especially) Legree are piling up the yards</p></div>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>⚾ <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-brewers-kept-reinventing-themselves\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Brewers Kept Reinventing Themselves Until They Were Champions </a></strong>- Following Milwaukee’s 5-game victory over Tampa Bay for the franchise’s first-ever World Series title, I wrote about how an incredible 11-2 October run capped off years of constant roster-churn and player development.</p>\n<ul><li><p>⚾ <strong>Related:</strong> <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-brewers-built-a-small-market\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Brewers Built a Small-Market Contender That Accidentally Became a Juggernaut</a></strong> - Another follow-up on Milwaukee’s World Series victory! I analyzed how the franchise evolved from a small-market team <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-2018-brewers-sure-look-a-lot?utm_source=publication-search\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">mimicking the 2010s Royals</a> into a powerhouse capable of sustaining long-term championship contention.</p></li></ul>\n</li>\n<li><p>⚾ <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/before-you-win-the-world-series-you\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Before You Win the World Series, You Get to Wear It </a></strong>- With jersey patches front and center in the 2026 Fall Classic, I looked into the surprisingly modern history of championship uniform-logos across major sports, and how they serve as a visual marker for the biggest games of the year.</p></li>\n<li><p>🏈 <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-vikings-are-winning-like-its\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The Vikings Are Winning Like It’s 1973</a></strong> - After wild Week 7 stumbles by Kansas City and San Francisco left Minnesota as the NFL’s sole remaining undefeated team in 2026, I broke down the throwback, defense-first style driving the Vikings’ unexpected run — and whether it can actually keep working in football’s modern era.</p></li>\n<li><p>⚾ <strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/the-world-series-is-closer-than-2\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">The World Series Is Closer Than 2-0 Looks. It May Not Matter for the Rays.</a></strong> - This requires some turning back the clock, but a pair of nail-biting, single-run Milwaukee wins did serve to open the 2026 Fall Classic. I tracked series Win Probabilities to explain why Tampa Bay found itself in a severe 2-0 hole despite how evenly-matched both games felt on the field.</p></li>\n<li><p>🏀 <strong><a href=\"https://www.espn.com/mens-college-basketball/story/_/id/50249218/mens-college-basketball-2026-27-preseason-storylines-predictions\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Men’s college hoops mega-preview: storylines, predictions, picks</a></strong> - Ahead of the 2026-27 Division I men’s college basketball tip-off, I helped ESPN’s college hoops crew to highlight the biggest storylines and project our picks for conference champions and Final Four contenders.</p></li>\n<li>\n<p>🏁 <strong><a href=\"https://www.nascar.com/news-media/2026/10/22/larsons-title-favorite-status-slips-ahead-of-talladega-as-bell-others-close-in/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Larson’s title-favorite status slips ahead of Talladega as Bell, others close in</a></strong> - Heading into Martinsville at  this week, I analyzed how Kyle Larson’s <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/2026-nascar-cup-series-driver-rankings\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">heavy title-favorite status</a> could still be upended through certain scenarios — albeit increasingly unlikely — that could see rivals Denny Hamlin, Christopher Bell, Chase Briscoe, Joey Logano, Ryan Blaney and Tyler Reddick steal the championship.</p>\n<ul><li><p>🏁🎙️ <strong><a href=\"https://open.spotify.com/episode/40pwPNVclW3NXbHSPvRtfN?si=x2A_BeaLSx-fpwm3Js6k-Q\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Podracing: Is It Over? (It Feels Over.)</a></strong> - In Episode No. 102 of , <a href=\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/tyler-lauletta-b0399667/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"> Lauletta</a> and I discussed Kyle Larson making all the right moves at Talladega — while almost all of his foes made the wrong ones — and whether the championship is effectively over. Then we made our betting and one-and-done picks for Martinsville, where The Paperclip could contain a big week for Team Penske.</p></li></ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>📊 Charts of the week:</h4>\n<p>Here were some of my favorite viz items of the week from <em><strong><a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/scoreboard-newsletter-archives\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Scoreboard</a></strong></em>, my daily newsletter for <a href=\"https://sherwood.news/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Sherwood News</a>… </p>\n<p><strong>🏁</strong><em><strong> On Kimi Antonelli <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/titles-on-the-line\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">potentially becoming</a> F1’s youngest champion…</strong></em></p>\n<div></div>\n<p>🏀<strong> </strong><em><strong>On the Atlanta Dream’s <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/titles-on-the-line\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">different paths to Finals wins</a>…</strong></em></p>\n<div class=\"reader-datawrapper\"><a href=\"https://datawrapper.dwcdn.net/CNXc7/1/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\"><img src=\"https://substack-post-media.s3.amazonaws.com/public/images/d3cac8cc-de74-4fe9-9d35-ebd94bfe81ee_1220x830.png\" alt=\"Three Atlanta wins, three different scoring advantages\" loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\"></a><p>Three Atlanta wins, three different scoring advantages</p></div>\n<p>🏀<strong> </strong><em><strong>On the <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/championship-brew\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">absurd start time</a> of Thursday’s potential WNBA clincher…</strong></em></p>\n<p>🏒<strong> </strong><em><strong>On Connor Hellebuyck’s <a href=\"https://neilpaine.substack.com/p/a-ring-deferred\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">performance in net relative to his new team</a>…</strong></em></p>\n<p><em>Subscribe to <strong>Scoreboard</strong> by <strong><a href=\"https://join.sherwood.news/scoreboard\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">clicking here</a></strong>!</em></p>\n<h4>👀 Some interesting things I read/watched this week</h4>\n<p><em>A collection of articles (with a heavy focus on my fellow Substackers), videos and other media that I enjoyed and/or found thought-provoking over the past week. I don’t always 100% agree with or endorse what’s linked here… but that’s also sort of the point.</em></p>\n<ul>\n<li><p><strong>🏈 <a href=\"https://throwbacks.substack.com/p/how-miami-forever-changed-college?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=31587&amp;post_id=222388742&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=false&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“How Miami Forever Changed College Football”</a> </strong>by  </p></li>\n<li><p><strong>🏈 <a href=\"https://www.unexpectedpoints.com/p/buffalo-we-have-a-defensive-problem?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=854340&amp;post_id=222785100&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Buffalo, We Have a (Defensive) Problem”</a></strong> by  </p></li>\n<li><p>🏈 <strong><a href=\"https://joonlee.substack.com/p/why-quarterbacks-have-to-be-boring?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=4580466&amp;post_id=222695756&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Why Quarterbacks Have To Be Boring” </a></strong>by  </p></li>\n<li><p>🏈<strong> <a href=\"https://www.splitzoneduo.com/p/jason-eck-new-mexico-lobos-team-of-the-week?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=2043967&amp;post_id=222397570&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Is This New Mexico’s Moment? Eck Yeah, Brother”</a></strong> by  </p></li>\n<li><p><strong>🏈 <a href=\"https://thespade.substack.com/p/the-middle-of-the-field-doesnt-exist?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=1892935&amp;post_id=222194360&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“The Middle of the Field Doesn’t Exist — But it will soon”</a> </strong>by  </p></li>\n<li><p><strong>🏈 <a href=\"https://bfarrell27.substack.com/p/the-big-12-is-imploding?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=459537&amp;post_id=222049856&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“The Big 12 is imploding”</a> </strong>by  </p></li>\n<li><p>🏈 <strong><a href=\"https://www.throwthedamball.com/p/has-caleb-williams-arrived?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=255229&amp;post_id=222437203&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“Has Caleb Williams Arrived?”</a></strong> by  </p></li>\n<li><p><strong>🏈 <a href=\"https://www.nflbluebook.com/p/week-7-recalibration-the-hyped-2027?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=10135524&amp;post_id=222261541&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“The hyped 2027 QB draft class has gotten messy. That’s bad for several NFL teams.”</a> </strong>by  </p></li>\n<li><p><strong>🏈 <a href=\"https://betweenthepipes.substack.com/p/nfl-games-are-more-exciting-and-longer?utm_source=post-email-title&amp;publication_id=1274895&amp;post_id=221945557&amp;utm_campaign=email-post-title&amp;isFreemail=true&amp;r=gwh9&amp;triedRedirect=true&amp;utm_medium=email\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">“NFL games are more exciting (and longer) than ever this season”</a